  "id": "absolute-refractory-period",
  "term": "absolute refractory period",
  "definition": "The absolute refractory period is the brief time after an action potential when a cell membrane is temporarily unable to respond to any new stimulus. During this phase, no stimulus can trigger another response as the membrane returns toward its resting, excitable state.",
